DISCUSSION
This is the classic AES-CTR keystream-reuse (many-time pad) vulnerability. Each plaintext line from `/tmp/exfil.txt` is encrypted with the *same* KEY and the *same* IV, and the counter is re-initialized to IV for every line. That means every ciphertext is XORed with an identical keystream. So `C1 XOR C2 = P1 XOR P2`, and I can attack this as a many-time pad.

Let me write a script to extract the base64 blocks and decode them.

